claim.claim-text:
a receiver (140);
a transmitter (144);
one or more processors (142) in communication with the receiver (140) and the transmitter (144); and
a memory in communication with the one or more processors (142), the memory comprising code that, when executed, causes the one or more processors to control the first base station to:

determine that the first base station (106) has available bandwidth to receive at least a portion of a first data stream sent from a source device (104) to a second base station on a wireless channel, wherein the first data stream is intended for a destination device (110) and the first data stream includes a code word comprising bits;
intercept (204) the at least a portion of the first data stream as a code shortened form of the first data stream, wherein the size of the at least a portion of the first data stream is based at least on the available bandwidth, and wherein the code shortened form of the first data stream comprises a shortened version of the code word that comprises a portion of the bits of the code word and is missing one or more bits of the code word; and
send (206) the code shortened form of the data stream to the destination device (110) as a second data stream (107).

a source device (102) configured to transmit a first data stream (103) including a code word comprising bits to a second base station (108);
the second base station (108) configured to send the first data steam (103) to a destination device;
a first base station (106) according to any of claims 1 to 13; and
the destination device (110) comprising:

a receiver (702);
one or more processors (708) in communication with the receiver; and,
memory (712) in communication with the one or more processors, the memory comprising code (718, 720, 722) that, when executed, causes the one or more processors to control the destination device to:

receive (302) the first data stream (103) from a network, the first data stream originating at the source device (104), being addressed to a the destination device (110) and including the code word comprising bits;
receive (302) the second data stream (107), wherein the second data stream includes the shortened version of the code word of the first data stream;
combine (210; 304) a redundant portion of the code word and a redundant portion of the shortened version of the code word to generate a third data stream; and,
provide the third data stream for processing.
